---
import {
  COMPETITORS,
  DRAFT_MINUTES,
  PARALLEL_MINUTES,
  RELEASE_VERSION,
  RESEARCH_MINUTES,
  SEQUENTIAL_MINUTES,
} from '../../consts/example';
import { PRODUCT_NAME } from '../../consts/product';
import { SNIPPETS } from '../../consts/snippets';
import { clock, listOf, minutes, minutesLong } from '../../lib/format';
import CodeCard from '../CodeCard.astro';
import DataTable from '../DataTable.astro';
import RaceDemo from '../demos/RaceDemo.astro';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Split from '../Split.astro';

const at = (minute: number) => clock(minute * 60);
const researchEnd = COMPETITORS.length * RESEARCH_MINUTES;

const comparison = [
  ...COMPETITORS.map((name, i) => [
    `Research ${name} (≈${minutes(RESEARCH_MINUTES)})`,
    `${at(i * RESEARCH_MINUTES)} → ${at((i + 1) * RESEARCH_MINUTES)}`,
    `${at(0)} → ${at(RESEARCH_MINUTES)}, in its own process`,
  ]),
  [
    'Draft the release notes',
    `${at(researchEnd)} → ${at(SEQUENTIAL_MINUTES)}`,
    `${at(0)} → ${at(DRAFT_MINUTES)}, while the research runs`,
  ],
  ['The user can use the chat', `after ${minutesLong(SEQUENTIAL_MINUTES)}`, `after about ${minutesLong(DRAFT_MINUTES)}`],
  ['The comparison is ready', `after ${minutesLong(SEQUENTIAL_MINUTES)}`, `after about ${minutesLong(PARALLEL_MINUTES)}`],
];
---

<Section id="features" heading="Do more at once, finish sooner">
  <h3 class="t-title">Run tools and sub-agents in parallel</h3>
  <p class="t-body">
    Every background task runs in its own process. When the model starts three tasks, all three run at the same time, and
    the agent doesn't sit idle while they do: it can keep working on the parts of the job that don't depend on them.
  </p>
  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <p class="t-body"><strong>An example.</strong> Your user asks:</p>
    <blockquote class="t-title quote">
      “Compare our pricing with {listOf(COMPETITORS)}, and draft the release notes for version {RELEASE_VERSION}.”
    </blockquote>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="after">
    <RaceDemo />
    <Split>
      <p class="t-lead">
        The longer and more independent the jobs, the bigger the gain: the agent finishes in the time of its slowest task,
        not the sum of all of them.
      </p>
      <p class="t-caption muted">
        Times are illustrative. How many tasks truly run at once depends on how you run them: one process each by default,
        or as many queue workers as you give them.
      </p>
      <DataTable slot="aside">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Step</span></th>
            <th scope="col">Without background tasks</th>
            <th scope="col">With {PRODUCT_NAME}</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            comparison.map(([step, without, withSubagents]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{step}</th>
                <td>{without}</td>
                <td>{withSubagents}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </DataTable>
    </Split>
    <Split class="divided">
      <h3 class="t-title">Sub-agents: specialists with a clean desk</h3>
      <p class="t-body">
        A <strong>sub-agent</strong> is a whole agent that your main agent can hand a job to: a researcher, a code reviewer, a
        data analyst. It gets only the instructions the main agent writes for it, not the whole conversation, so it starts
        focused and doesn't fill the main conversation with its intermediate steps. The main agent reads its final report.
      </p>
      <p class="t-body">
        The model sees a tool called <code class="ic">researcher</code> with one argument, <code class="ic">prompt</code>.
        <code class="ic">ResearchAgent</code> is any agent of yours: nothing in it is specific to this package.
      </p>
      <CodeCard slot="aside" title="PHP" snippet={SNIPPETS.subagent} />
    </Split>
  </Fragment>
</Section>

<style lang="scss">
  .quote {
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }

  .divided {
    padding-top: var(--space-12);
    border-top: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-line);
  }
</style>
